From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wangra <wangra@google.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 11:50:56 -0400
Subject: GL/D3D11: Clamp multiview-adjusted attribute divisor

Scale vertex attribute divisor in 64-bit and clamp to GLuint max when
emulating multiview. This prevents integer overflow wrapping large
divisors to zero and causing validation-driver state desynchronization.

Test: angle_end2end_tests --gtest_filter="*MultiviewRenderTest.LargeAttribDivisor*"
Bug: b/536544435
Change-Id: Ifbda72d7a0c11f3ca0287e2d25e3d2ab3d5c682e
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8194046
Reviewed-by: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Ran Wang <wangra@google.com>

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y): Prerequisite for cherry-pick-48a16bd63d2d (adds GetMultiviewAdjustedDivisor). The GL backend's local GetAdjustedDivisor helper was removed as upstream did; call sites use the shared helper.

